{"name":"Rocket Man","hex":"#bebec3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rocket","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A projectile.\nA cylindrical projectile that can be fired to a great height through combustion,  a type of firework of this form, typically exploding with light and colour; a skyrocket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\nA blunt lance head used in jousting.\nA long vehicle or craft propelled by a rocket engine; a missile or rocket-propelled spacecraft. \n\nAn engine operating similarly to the pyrotechnic, generating thrust by the expulsion of hot gases; a rocket engine.","A cylindrical projectile that can be fired to a great height through combustion,  a type of firework of this form, typically exploding with light and colour; a skyrocket. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To accelerate swiftly and powerfully.","To fly vertically."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rocket"},{"term":"man","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-3 language code for Mandingo."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male human.","All human males collectively: mankind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/man"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rocket","blocks":[{"text":"A rocket is an elongated flying vehicle that uses a rocket engine to accelerate without using any surrounding air. A rocket engine produces thrust by reaction to exhaust expelled at high speed. Unlike jet engines, rockets are fuelled entirely by propellant which they carry, without the need for oxygen from air; consequently a rocket can fly in the vacuum of space, and indeed rocket engines operate more efficiently outside the atmosphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Soyuz_TMA-9_launch.jpg/330px-Soyuz_TMA-9_launch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket"},{"title":"Astronaut","blocks":[{"text":"An astronaut is a person trained, equipped, and deployed by a human spaceflight program to serve as a commander or crew member of a spacecraft. Although generally reserved for professional space travelers, the term is sometimes applied to anyone who travels into space, including scientists, politicians, journalists, and space tourists. In the United States, it is a designated term used by three agencies: NASA, the FAA, and the military. The term is also used for people who are trained to fly in a spacecraft after passing certain training courses, regardless of their experience of space travel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Bruce_McCandless_II_during_EVA_in_1984.jpg/330px-Bruce_McCandless_II_during_EVA_in_1984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronaut"},{"title":"Rocket Man (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rocket Man\", also known as \"Rocket Man \", is a song written by British musician Elton John and lyricist Bernie Taupin, and performed by John. It was originally released on 31 March 1972 in the US, as the lead single to John's album Honky Château. The song first charted in the UK on 22 April, rising to No. 2 in the UK singles chart and No. 6 in the US Billboard Hot 100, becoming a major hit single for John. It is considered to be John's signature song."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Rocket_man_by_elton_john_US_single_variant_B.png/330px-Rocket_man_by_elton_john_US_single_variant_B.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rocket_Man_(song)"},{"title":"Man","blocks":[{"text":"A man is an adult male human. Before adulthood, a male child or adolescent is referred to as a boy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Outdoors-man-portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Outdoors-man-portrait_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg/330px-Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg/330px-Oldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rocket arrows depicted in the Huolongjing: \"fire arrow\", \"dragon-shaped arrow frame\", and a \"complete fire arrow\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOldest_depiction_of_rocket_arrows.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rocket_warfare.jpg/500px-Rocket_warfare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Rocket_warfare.jpg/500px-Rocket_warfare.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mysorean rockets and rocket artillery used to defeat an East India Company battalion during the Battle of Guntur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARocket_warfare.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg/250px-William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c0/William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg/250px-William_Congreve_at_Copenhagen_1807.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" William Congreve at the